# A generic layout (no dataset named) with one 3D view per file, as the browser's Save Layout writes it for a session
# that opened each file in its own view: both files carry /tf, each view also reads a topic only its own file carries
# (/robot_description, /costmap). A scene binds as a whole, so its /tf follows its own topic: nothing is ambiguous, and
# no dataset is asked for or chosen (pj_app ARCHITECTURE "One layout over several datasets"). The robot view's /tf
# itself stays pending (ARCHITECTURE "Known gaps": a local robot model gives the view no dataset to prefer), so this
# checks only that no dataset was chosen. Both data files are committed browser fixtures.
# app: -d tests/wasm/fixtures/ros2_robot_description_real.mcap -d tests/wasm/fixtures/ros2_occupancy_real.mcap -l scripts/qa/regressions/fixtures/scene3d_tf_two_views.pj4.xml
# needs: plugins
until get_status {} "ros2_occupancy_real.mcap"
until ui_tree {} PJ::Scene3DDockWidget
# A dataset chosen for the layout reads "Warning | Layout | Layout '<file>' fits 2 loaded datasets". Filtered first,
# since the list shows only the rows in its viewport.
ui_click {"name":"buttonNotifications","wait_ms":500}
ui_click {"name":"searchBox","wait_ms":200}
ui_type {"text":"Layout","wait_ms":500}
ui_tree {}
expect QLineEdit "Layout"
expect | Info | Layout | Loaded layout
absent | Warning | Layout | Layout '
ui_key {"keys":"Escape"}
